# typescript-eslint (as of 8.70.1, still the latest published release) hard-
# blocks TypeScript 7 and declares a `typescript: >=4.8.4 <6.1.0` peer range,
# so a strict npm install/ci conflicts with this repo's TypeScript 7
# devDependency. The actual TS 6 copy typescript-eslint runs against is
# `typescript-for-eslint` (aliased in package.json), wired up via
# node_modules symlinks in scripts/link-ts-for-eslint.mjs (the postinstall
# script) -- this flag just lets npm finish resolving the tree despite the
# declared peer mismatch. Tracking issue for real TS7 support:
# https://github.com/typescript-eslint/typescript-eslint/issues/10940
legacy-peer-deps=true
